       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Having spent sometime with the HttpResourceConverter I am now thinking that we could just store the internal references as literal URIs, but without the baseUri stuff (<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/</a> for example). Then we could just build the URI by passing that path to the normally configured UriInfo.baseUriBuilder and get a full URI.</p>\n\n<p>Which is a long way of saying that maybe this could be dropped.</p>",
     "created": "20/Apr/18 4:12 PM",
